an effect row whole (gathered_to_his_people): {'en': "gathered to his people — the STATUS the death notice writes: 'and he expired and was gathered to his people' — the formula at Abraham (25:8), Ishmael (25:17), Isaac (35:29), and Jacob (49:33; 49:29 'I am being gathered' in his own mouth), each followed by a burial by sons; 'he expired' at the four patriarchal deaths and the flood (7:21); the sons' burial-duty opens at the gathering", 'he': 'וַיִּגְוַע וַיֵּאָסֶף אֶל עַמָּֽיו (and he expired and was gathered to his people — Gen 49:33)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Gen 49:33, 49:29 ('I am being gathered to my people'), 25:8, 25:17, 35:29 ('and was gathered to his people' — the Genesis seats, measured), 7:21, 25:8, 25:17, 35:29, 49:33 ('and he expired' — five Genesis seats), 50:1-3 (the weeping and the embalming — by name); Num 20:24, 27:13, Deut 32:50 (Aaron and Moses — by name); Babylonian Talmud Taanit 31a:4, Bava Batra 16b:18-17a:1 (the three who tasted the world to come); Mishnah Avot 4:22 by name; (O8 S3, 2026-09-08) Gen 25:8 (Abraham), 25:17 (Ishmael) written by law_mamre beside the family engine's 49:33; (O8 S4, 2026-09-08) Gen 35:29 (Isaac, old and full of days) written by law_joseph", 'corpus': 'gen_72_testament_twelve (STEP_Gn_49_29, 49_33)', 'exam': "cold_run_family.py (testament — the scene's last event)"} | (go_up_to_nebo_see_the_land_commanded): {'en': "go up to Nebo and see the land, commanded — the STATUS the line nebo_summons_die_as_aaron writes on Moses: 'GO UP INTO THIS MOUNTAIN OF ABARIM, MOUNT NEBO, which is in the land of Moab, that is over against Jericho, AND BEHOLD THE LAND OF CANAAN which I give to the children of Israel for a possession' (32:49) — Numbers 27:12's five in order, ten tokens shared: THE COMMISSION'S MOUNTAIN (opening_speech.the_commission by CALL — one mountain, three names: Abarim, Nebo, Pisgah; the debit see_the_land_from_abarim OPEN BY DESIGN to 34:1-4 — the summons its second telling, a REFERENCE by the ink's own words, the debit not closed here); 355:6 Reuben's portion (gad_reuben's moses_grave by CALL — Reuben's Nebo, Gad's field); the land of Canaan (borders by reference); Avot 5:6 the twilight creations (a parameter)", 'he': 'עֲלֵה אֶל הַר הָעֲבָרִים הַזֶּה הַר נְבוֹ (go up into this mountain of Abarim, Mount Nebo — Deut 32:49)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 32:49, 3:27 (opening_speech — Pisgah, the reference); Numbers 27:12 (opening_speech — the commission's debit, the reference); Numbers 32:38 (gad_reuben — Nebo, the reference); Numbers 34:2 (borders — the land of Canaan, the reference); Mishnah Avot 5:6 (read whole at the design); Onkelos 32:49; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 338, 355:6, 37:11", 'corpus': 'deu_32_haazinu (STEP_Dt_32_1 through STEP_Dt_32_43; claims DV32-01 through DV32-12) and deu_32_song_aftermath (STEP_Dt_32_44 through STEP_Dt_32_52; claims DV32A-01 through DV32A-04)', 'exam': 'cold_run_song_charge_nebo.py (F15 the_summons_to_nebo — go_up_into_this_mountain_of_abarim_mount_nebo_and_behold_the_land_of_canaan; the line nebo_summons_die_as_aaron) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the twenty-six Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_32_haazinu_exam_2026-09-28.md)'} | (see_the_land_from_afar_not_go_there): {'en': "see the land from afar, not go there — the HEAVEN entry the line meribah_trespass_not_go_there_declared writes on Moses: 'FOR YOU SHALL SEE THE LAND BEFORE YOU, BUT THERE YOU SHALL NOT GO, into the land which I give to the children of Israel' (32:52) — ONCE in this form; 34:4's 'there you shall not cross' the kin AHEAD (341:1 and 357:27 set 32:52's 'go' against 34:4's 'cross' — THE FOUR DENIALS: not as king nor commoner, not alive nor dead; 34:4 cited never read — READ THEN COMPILE PER PORTION, a pointer row OWED to the next sitting); the seeing granted and the entering denied — the sentence's positive arm with its bar; 3:27's Pisgah the retelling READ BACK by opening_speech; THE CHAPTER'S CLOSE", 'he': 'כִּי מִנֶּגֶד תִּרְאֶה אֶת הָאָרֶץ וְשָׁמָּה לֹא תָבוֹא (for you shall see the land before you, but there you shall not go — Deut 32:52)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': 'Deut 32:52, 3:27 (opening_speech — Pisgah, the reference), 34:4 (AHEAD — cited, never read); Numbers 27:12-13 (opening_speech — the reference); Onkelos 32:52; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 341, 357:27', 'corpus': 'deu_32_haazinu (STEP_Dt_32_1 through STEP_Dt_32_43; claims DV32-01 through DV32-12) and deu_32_song_aftermath (STEP_Dt_32_44 through STEP_Dt_32_52; claims DV32A-01 through DV32A-04)', 'exam': 'cold_run_song_charge_nebo.py (F16 meribah_and_the_seeing — you_shall_see_the_land_before_you_but_there_you_shall_not_go; the line meribah_trespass_not_go_there_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the twenty-six Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_32_haazinu_exam_2026-09-28.md)'} | (holy_people_promised): {'en': "a holy people promised — the HEAVEN entry the line covenant_formula_declared writes on Israel: 'and that you be A HOLY PEOPLE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD, as He spoke' (26:19) — 'a holy people' 7:6, 14:2 (seven_nations.the_holy_people, food_tithe by CALL — the references) and 28:9 ahead (the conditional's seat, this runner's own line); 'AS HE SPOKE' the second AS_WHEN pointer — a RUN CITATION of 7:6 and 14:2; Onkelos 'a holy people BEFORE the LORD'; conditional in blessings_for_hearing's form", 'he': 'וְלִֽהְיֹתְךָ עַם קָדֹשׁ לַיהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ (and that you be a holy people to the LORD your God — Deut 26:19)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': "Deut 26:19, 7:6, 14:2 (the holy people's seats, the run citation), 28:9 (this runner's own line); Exodus 19:6 (the holy nation); Onkelos 26:19", 'corpus': 'deu_26_bikkurim_close (STEP_Dt_26_1 through STEP_Dt_26_19; claims DV26-01 through DV26-03), deu_27_ebal_curses (STEP_Dt_27_1 through STEP_Dt_27_26; claims DV27-01 through DV27-04), deu_28_blessings (STEP_Dt_28_1 through STEP_Dt_28_14; claims DV28A-01 through DV28A-04), deu_28_curses_a (STEP_Dt_28_15 through STEP_Dt_28_44; claims DV28B-01 through DV28B-05) and deu_28_curses_b (STEP_Dt_28_45 through STEP_Dt_28_69; claims DV28C-01 through DV28C-05)', 'exam': 'cold_run_firstfruits_ebal_curses.py (F3 the_covenant_formula — high_above_all_nations_a_holy_people_as_he_spoke; the line covenant_formula_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the twenty-six Mishnah rows the ledger cites (deu_26_28_ki_tavo_exam_2026-09-26.md)'} | (rain_in_its_season): {'en': "the rain in its season — the conditional HEAVEN entry the line second_paragraph_declared writes on Israel (blessings_for_hearing's form — 7:12's conditional; treasured_people's, Exodus 19:5): 'if you hearken, hearken to My commandments … I WILL GIVE THE RAIN OF YOUR LAND IN ITS SEASON, THE EARLY RAIN AND THE LATE RAIN, and you shall gather your grain, your wine and your oil; and I will give grass in your field for your cattle, and you shall eat and be satisfied' (11:13-15) — Leviticus 26:4's 'I will give your rains in their season' (tochacha.covenant by CALL) with THE TWO NAMED RAINS ADDED: THE VALUE FROM THE SHELF — 'in its season' THE FREE VARIABLE AFTER THE DECREE (Rosh Hashanah 17b:11-13: the rain decreed at the head of the year cannot be added to or reduced, but falls in season on the land that needs it for good, out of season on forests and deserts for bad; the year judged at its head from 11:12's 'from the beginning of the year to its end', 8a:16, 16b:12); the early rain in Marcheshvan and the late in Nisan (Ta'anit 6a:5, 6a:7 — 'in its due time'; the early rain's three dates the 3rd, the 7th and the 17th, 6a:3; both for a blessing); THE RAIN ASKED IN THE SERVICE OF THE HEART — 11:13's 'to serve Him with all your heart' is prayer and 11:14's rain follows it (Ta'anit 2a:11; the mention in the resurrection blessing and the request in the years' blessing, both indispensable — Berakhot 33a:11, 33a:29; the dates the parameter rain_dates); the cattle before the man — 'grass for your cattle' then 'you shall eat and be satisfied' (Berakhot 40a:1, Gittin 62a:16); rain for one man, one field, one plant (Ta'anit 9b:3-4); the Land watered by the Holy One Himself, first (10a:2-3); 28:12's 'to give the rain of your land in its season' the pair forward", 'he': 'וְנָתַתִּי מְטַֽר אַרְצְכֶם בְּעִתּוֹ (and I will give the rain of your land in its season — Deut 11:14)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': "Deut 11:13-15 (the condition, the rain, the grain, the cattle, the eating); Deut 11:10-12 (the land drinking by the rain of heaven, the eyes of the LORD from the year's beginning to its end), 28:12 (the pair forward), 28:24 (the curse's pair); Leviticus 26:3-5 (the rains in their season — the cell by CALL), 26:19-20; Deut 7:13 (the grain, wine and oil — seven_nations by CALL); Onkelos 11:14; Babylonian Talmud Ta'anit 2a:1-3, 2a:11, 3b:6, 6a:3-7, 7a:2, 8b:5, 9b:3-4, 9b:10-11, 10a:2-3, 10a:11-16; Rosh Hashanah 8a:16, 16b:3, 16b:12, 17b:11-13; Berakhot 33a:11-15, 33a:29, 40a:1, 55a:9; Gittin 62a:16; Bava Batra 19a:18; Mishnah Ta'anit 1:1-5 (through the Gemara); the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 37-42", 'corpus': 'deu_11_bless_curse_set (STEP_Dt_11_13 through STEP_Dt_11_15; the claims DV11-01 through DV11-06)', 'exam': "cold_run_blessing_and_curse.py (F3 the_second_paragraph — if_you_hearken, the_rain_in_its_season, the_early_and_the_late, the_rains_dates, the_cattle_first, the_prayer_from_the_clause; F2 the_land_watered_by_heaven — the_decree_and_the_season; the exam kind blessing_curse_case; the entry written on the tape kind second_paragraph_declared at the counter's day)", 'second_seat': "THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 18b (2026-09-26) — the conditional HEAVEN entry REUSED at Deut 28:12 by law_firstfruits_ebal_curses on israel_people (the line heavens_treasure_lending_declared: 'the LORD will open to you His good treasure, the heavens, to give the rain of your land in its season' — the rain state's blessing seat, the Sifrei 40:12 with 11:17 the shutting; 306:6 'open' is widen); the row 11:14 above the first seat"} | (length_of_days_on_the_land_promised): {'en': "the length of days on the land promised — the conditional HEAVEN entry the line life_and_death_choice_declared writes on Israel: 'for HE IS YOUR LIFE AND THE LENGTH OF YOUR DAYS, that you may dwell in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac and to Jacob, to give them' (30:20) — the promise's own words; 4:40's, 5:16's, 11:9's prolonging the kin; the oath to the three fathers a relative clause, not the AS_WHEN form (hear_o_israel.the_gift_and_the_warning by CALL — no pointer predicted); the readback row 30:19 SUPPLIED with the writes and the two reuses", 'he': 'כִּי הוּא חַיֶּיךָ וְאֹרֶךְ יָמֶיךָ (for He is your life and the length of your days — Deut 30:20)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': 'Deut 30:20, 4:40 (obey_horeb), 5:16 (covenant_at_horeb), 11:9 (blessing_and_curse — the prolonging, the reference), 6:10 (hear_o_israel — the oath of the land); Onkelos 30:20', 'corpus': 'deu_29_moab_covenant (STEP_Dt_29_1 through STEP_Dt_29_28; claims DV29-01 through DV29-05), deu_30_teshuvah_choice (STEP_Dt_30_1 through STEP_Dt_30_20; claims DV30-01 through DV30-04) and deu_31_charge_torah (STEP_Dt_31_1 through STEP_Dt_31_30; claims DV31-01 through DV31-06)', 'exam': 'cold_run_covenant_return_charge.py (F9 life_and_death — choose_life_love_hearken_and_cleave_the_length_of_days; the line life_and_death_choice_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the seven Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_29_31_nitzavim_vayelech_exam_2026-09-27.md)', 'second_seat': "THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 20b (2026-09-28) — the HEAVEN entry REUSED at Deut 32:47 by law_song_charge_nebo on israel_people (the line set_your_heart_no_empty_matter_declared: 'and through this thing you shall prolong your days on the land which you cross the Jordan to possess' — 11:9's five in order; the reward's two arms, the fruit here and the days there); 30:20 the first seat (covenant_return_charge's line life_and_death_choice_declared)"}
