 parameter rows whole (the death date, the pilgrimages): [('the_prophets_death', {'era': 'exodus', 'idiom': 'the_prophets_death', 'value': {'stoning': "the Sifrei's majority and the Rabbis at Sanhedrin 89b:15-19 — by the analogy (I2, checked in MIDDOT.md) of 'thrust' (13:6 'to thrust you from the way' / 13:11 'he sought to thrust you'): as the inciter is stoned, so the false prophet who preaches idolatry (the Sifrei 86:6, 90:2 the analogy run back)", 'strangling': "R. Shimon (the Sifrei 86:6) and MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 11:1's list of the strangled — THE ANSWER SHEET'S ARM: an unspecified death in the Torah is strangling (89b:20-21; the Rambam's Introduction 5:2 — 'witnesses testifying, strangled'); the false prophet's table at 90a:2-6 says strangled for the essence abolished", 'the_default': "the answer sheet's — strangling (Mishnah 11:1); the runner's case writes put_to_death ('mode per the compiled law') beside evil_purged_from_the_midst; the stoning arm the Sifrei's, recorded"}, 'boundary': "two arms recorded, not resolved — the DATA row of the compile; the exam's persons take the answer sheet's arm; the inciter's stoning (13:11) written in ink, no parameter", 'channel': 'received', 'source': "Deut 13:6, 13:11; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 86:6, 90:2; Mishnah Sanhedrin 11:1, 11:5-6; Babylonian Talmud Sanhedrin 89b:15-21, 90a:2-6, 67a:7-8, 84a:14; the Rambam's Introduction to the Mishnah 5:2", 'teacher': 'Sanhedrin 89b:15-21', 'exercised_by': ['seducers']}), ('isaacs_death_after_the_sale', {'value': 'twelve_years', 'settings': {'twelve_years': "died:isaac (35:28: a hundred and eighty) twelve years after Joseph's sale at seventeen — 180 − 60 (25:26) − 91 − 17"}, 'channel': 'derived', 'source': "Gen 35:28, 25:26, 41:46, 45:6, 47:9, 37:2 — the ink's own arithmetic: the page order (35:29 before 37:2) against the chronology (the sale before the death), the proleptic marker of 35:28 carrying it (CJ2)", 'teacher': "the ink's arithmetic", 'exercised_by': ['sequence']}), ('the_death_date_of_moses', {'era': 'exodus', 'idiom': 'the_death_date_of_moses', 'value': {'the_year': "THE FORTIETH YEAR OF THE EXODUS ERA — THE INK'S: 'Moses was eighty years old when he spoke to Pharaoh' (Exodus 7:7 — the tape's own line) + the forty years of the wilderness = the hundred and twentieth year (31:2's [120] the parser's own number; 34:7's the death's — sitting 22's); Genesis 6:3's hundred and twenty the number's Genesis seat (a reference, no transfer)", 'the_day': "THE SEVENTH OF ADAR — THE ANSWER SHEET'S: Tosefta Sotah 11:3 read whole at the design — 'this day' teaches his years were completed to the day; computed BACKWARD from Joshua 4:19's tenth of Nisan (the people up from the Jordan) by the thirty days' weeping (34:8) and the three days' preparation (Joshua 1:11) — thirty-three days; Seder Olam 10:2 as chukat.edom_and_hor('death_dates') holds it; the Sifrei 2:3's 'completed to the hour'", 'the_month': "ADAR THE TWELFTH MONTH AS THE CLOCK COUNTS IT — whether the fortieth year was intercalated the shelf does not say (the_intercalated_month a PARAMETER — 2:3's row: 1 Kings 4:19's one officer; sitting 14b's intercalation parameter the kin)", 'the_marker': "THE STITCHER'S ROW — placed AT 31:1 (the line crossing_charge_declared's first verse; Genesis 7:1's precedent: the number at 7:4, the position 7:1), the number's verse 31:2 named in its value; the 9 lines of chapters 29-30 at (40, 11, 1) before it, the 11 of chapter 31 at (40, 12, 7) after it; 32:48's 'that same day' and 34:5's death stand on this day"}, 'boundary': "THE MARKER — the counter's day moves from 1:3's (40, 11, 1) to (40, 12, 7), the first forward date in Deuteronomy since 1:3 and the first marker of the walk since chapter 10's retrograde pair; markers 172 -> 173 (read from the print)", 'channel': 'received', 'source': 'Deut 31:2, 31:14, 31:16, 31:22 (the same day), 32:48, 34:5-8; Exodus 7:7; Genesis 6:3; Joshua 1:11, 4:19; Tosefta Sotah 11:3; Seder Olam 10:2; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 2:3', 'teacher': 'Tosefta Sotah 11:3', 'exercised_by': ['covenant_return_charge']})]
